5. Implement std::vector Internals
Design a simplified Vector<T> class that manages dynamic memory, supports push_back, reserve, resize, copy/move semantics, and strong exception safety guarantees.

2. Build a Thread-Safe Bounded Queue
Implement a bounded blocking queue using condition variables and mutexes. The queue should support multiple producers and consumers. Ensure there are no deadlocks, missed wakeups, or spurious wakeup bugs.

14. Implement a Spin Lock and Compare with Mutex
Design a spin lock using atomic_flag. Benchmark and explain when spin locks outperform mutexes and when they degrade performance.




1. Implement a Fixed-Size Memory Pool Allocator
Design and implement a fixed-size memory pool that pre-allocates a large chunk of memory and serves fixed-size object allocations in O(1) time. The allocator must avoid fragmentation and support deallocation. Discuss cache locality and alignment concerns.

4. Design a Thread Pool from Scratch
Implement a thread pool that supports task submission, graceful shutdown, and work stealing. Ensure exception safety and proper resource cleanup.




7. Build a Custom Hash Map
Implement a hash map using open addressing or separate chaining. Handle collisions, resizing, rehashing, and iterator validity.

11. Build a LRU Cache
Design a thread-safe LRU cache with O(1) get and put operations using a combination of hash map and doubly linked list. Ensure correctness under concurrent access.







3. Implement a Lock-Free Stack
Design a lock-free stack using atomic operations and compare-and-swap (CAS). Explain the ABA problem and implement a mitigation strategy (e.g., version tagging).

10. Implement a Lock-Free Ring Buffer
Design a single-producer, single-consumer ring buffer optimized for low latency. Use atomic operations and memory barriers correctly.






6. Implement a Custom std::function
Build a type-erased callable wrapper that can store lambdas, function pointers, and functors. Implement small buffer optimization to avoid heap allocation for small callables.


8. Implement Double-Checked Locking Singleton
Design a singleton using double-checked locking and explain why memory ordering matters. Provide a correct implementation using C++11 atomics.

9. Implement RAII Wrapper for File Descriptor
Design a class that safely manages POSIX file descriptors. Implement move semantics, prevent copying, and ensure exception-safe cleanup.



12. Implement Copy-on-Write String
Design a string class that shares memory between copies and performs deep copy only on mutation. Ensure thread-safety considerations are clearly discussed.

13. Design a Smart Logger
Create a high-performance asynchronous logger using a lock-free queue and a dedicated logging thread. Ensure minimal latency impact on producer threads.


